{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: R7 certified Rules hardening. Head 18573b4109ac79783092bc4e4da26a440ca8827c, tree ea5d7ea1, branch request/r7-hardening-20261026: Main 9efe36a3 is the merge base, 60 paths change (1,890 insertions, 116 deletions). Review request 40a1b23f, checker promise 862a66b4, request 5e6d482c, planner decision e17cbaa4, ruling db8052fa. Primary artifact fe638a59 (the PD-2 note), first of 63 artifacts at this head.\n\nRead order: the note in full; 5e6d482c, e17cbaa4 and db8052fa; every production path in the delta (rules-scope-v12, rules-certificate-v15, destination-v15, destination-budget-v15, reservation-v15, the G15 branches of destination.ts, floor.ts, destination-host.ts, the catalog, versions, archive policy and bindings, CLI, Page); the witness tests and fixture; the four paired-control outputs and the final gate record. I did not run any suite again.\n\nThe request's four items, each with its witness:\n1. Record size. G15 ties the passes record to the scope's real Bounds.entryBytes (certifiedPublicationBudgetV15: ceiling = entryBytes minus the largest future fence or check-completion envelope). Before the first capture it reserves all 32 proof rows at maximum width. certifiedPublicationStateV15 refuses any value whose reserve does not fit. destination.ts refuses a capture that cannot fit with not-reserved and reason evidence-too-large, before it stores passes; this applies both when the record decoder refuses and when the complete-envelope forecast refuses. The forecast lowers ref effects to the longer value form and saturates numbers and times. The observation reserve of 76 records (plus 75 separators) matches the judge's five declared rows: rules 1, key 1, holders 1, member 65, second key 8. The witness admits the largest constructed capture, refuses the next one 2 bytes over, stores 32 real check proofs and replays consistently. Final-gate figures (single run): largest entry 88,072 bytes, 32-proof record 83,907, actual capture 63,903 against 262,144. This is the \"tie to the bound\" option of item 1, and the note says so. It also says that the boundary is maximal only within its padding construction.\n2. Liveness. A named certificate-declined value with request and interveningFact, at most 1,024 bytes, covers all three windows: native beforeSend (no provider read), the host check after the held read, and the final race, where selection fails because the head moved and derives recomputes the decline. In every window native code derives interveningFact from the scope's own current head and does not use the host's claimed fact. wellFormed rejects a host decline whose intervening position is not above the request and at most the current head, so the host cannot invent a decline while the Destination is quiet. In the final race the confirmed host evidence is kept unchanged (selected:false). The three boundary tests show this with two real intervening signed entries, and the final-race case replays consistent. The entry-flood limit is recorded, as 5e6d482c asked.\n3. Reuse. Q12 keeps one monotone marker: the same full Destination reference (scope, incarnation, kind) and a strictly greater request position. It commits in the same effect as the policy. Equal gives rules-certificate-used, older gives rules-certificate-stale, and invalid stored provenance fails closed. The witness publishes, refuses the same certificate as used, publishes a fresh one and refuses the first as stale. The scope item is unchanged after each refusal. This is e17cbaa4 item 3 as accepted.\n4. Page. Q11 and Q12 are read-only, writes refuse before signing (test.each over 11 and 12), and the text is \"No user-facing publish command is available yet.\"\n\nAuthority-chain four facts (the note's list) hold at the head:\n1. Sibling births: rulesCertificateFamilyV15 authenticates the Directory 19, Membership 8, Rules 12 and Destination 15 genesis entries by pin, seed, ordinal, cause and the Directory's own send. It binds directory, membership, rules and branch across the siblings, requires ownerMayReview false, and requires the signer's membership to be the family's.\n2. Exact opening: rulesCertificateOpeningV15 accepts only a single-attempt G15 operation, with one operation effect, one opened attempt and one request snapshot, whose binding names this Destination and the signed proposal.\n3. Retained policy and tree proof: the policy is read by digest under its domain and bound, and verifyRulesTree checks the proof against the opening's binding and the policy's patterns, both at selection and at publication.\n4. Confirmed selected outcome: rulesPublishedCertificateV15 requires an outcome of owner destination@15, attempt 1, result confirmed and selected true, at the position directly after the request (prev equals the request hash), with evidence equal to the proposal, proof and started. The opening's birth references must equal the authenticated siblings. A caller-supplied digest or host flag is never enough.\n\nPaired controls (raw outputs read). Each control's original line is present once at the control commit and once at the head. The witness files and fixture are unchanged from each control commit to the head. Production changes after the last control commit (1c38e616) are none, except the regenerated Page asset.\n- reuse (1d5cab9f): the used check is disabled, and the Q12 test fails because the reused certificate is accepted; 3 other tests pass.\n- decline (7665c2ed): finalRace is disabled, and only the heldAnswer test fails (no decline value).\n- budget (1c38e616): the capture admission is disabled, and the budget witness fails.\n- floor (d81c7a10): the G15 floor branch is disabled, and the retained positions drop from [17, 18, 49] to [17, 49].\n\nFloor and historical pins: the floor hook acts only on the exact G15 type mark and genesis pin, and keeps the request and intervening positions of the current decline record. Every Destination 14 path keeps its own owner string, decoder and floor roots. Q11, G14, R19 and D18 are unchanged. D19 has the same data digest as D18 and differs in its rules (child pins and ownerMayReview false); all lookups are by pin, so the shared digest is safe.\n\nValidation:\n- The first gate (04ed601d) failed on seal literals, and the native follow-up (1a06191b) failed on V8 heap exhaustion. Both stay recorded as failures.\n- The repairs changed only test files: the 12 seal literals, and the fixed clock in maintained-application-projections.test.ts. A plain fixed Date.now replaces the recording spy, the prior function is restored, and every assertion and 30-second deadline stays.\n- The parser candidate was withdrawn: packages/bytes has no change from a51b0ac3 to the head.\n- The fresh ordinary gate at 1c502505 (tree 58ce7107) passed: exit 0, 876.985 s wall, 1,857.051 s child CPU (one run). Node 57, Counting 55, plain 2,848 passed and 1 skipped, Native 786 passed and 2 skipped, no unhandled errors, no contradictory records.\n- Only the note and the manifest change after the gate, so the documents-only rule applies and no second gate is owed. The note names the gate of record and labels the heap figures as one-run observations, as db8052fa asked.\n- Evidence: the manifest verifies against the raw directory: 287 files, 0 bad, nothing writable, SHA256SUMS all OK. check-notes 9efe36a3..18573b41 reports 0 warnings, and git diff --check is clean.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The family is explicit and additive (R20, D19, M8, Q12, G15, I1) behind --cohort hardened-certified-rules. The default creation cohort (ARCHIVE_DEVICE_PUBLICATION_COHORT) and every PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS setting are unchanged, so no deployment can create the new family until the planner schedules it. There is no kernel or outcome-contract change, as e17cbaa4 required. Kernel section 7.1: this head adds new versions of existing platform definitions; the planner should confirm that K1's count records them.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding.\n- The record cannot become unwritable under its retained bounds.\n- A certificate is one-use without a history scan.\n- Declines are native facts, not host claims.\n- Selection still needs the head to equal the opening.\n- The deliberate entry-flood liveness limit remains and is recorded.\n- The rules-certificate-destination-mismatch refusal has no witness. It appears unreachable, because the family check already pins the request to the one authenticated Destination sibling. It is a defensive check.\n\nSimplification: acceptable. reservation-v15.ts is a 184-line copy of reservation-v14.ts that differs only in the rules definition name and type names. A definition parameter would remove the copy without changing V14. That is a candidate for BR-13's version tables, not a gap in this head. The memory investigation stays out of the delivered tree.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head 18573b41. The builder lands. No deployment or cohort activation is requested; the planner schedules the cohort.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fe638a5932dcf4d5c2aa437c4ba99f70b75cbcab","binding":"assigned","head":"18573b4109ac79783092bc4e4da26a440ca8827c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:862a66b4486313a9a6696a52d1842ccfc666870b\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f82aba226d8ef77d53c616dfb622a5acbbea3f51\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:862a66b4486313a9a6696a52d1842ccfc666870b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}